Gold Band editor: a failure target is not an entry candidate

deriveWorkflowEntryCandidateIds ignored every non-success edge that sorts
backward in the success topology, so a node reached only by a failure edge
(a human check after a failed round) could count as a second entry whenever its
id sorted before the failing node. Save, run-mode start and task-list start
refuse such a workflow ("multiple entry nodes").

A backward non-success edge is now ignored only when it closes a loop: the
target reaches the source over success edges (a retry back to the entry, kept
as before). Any other failure edge counts as an incoming edge. A node with no
incoming edge at all is still an entry, and a workflow with none still errors.

